#! The clean case. `hello.lu` compiles, so the server must publish an EMPTY
#! diagnostics array rather than staying silent — a client that never hears
#! about a file it opened cannot tell "no problems" from "not analysed yet",
#! and both tier-0 editors render the difference identically (nothing).
name      diagnostics/clean-file
profile   minimal

initialize
open      hello.lu
wait      diagnostics hello.lu
shutdown
